    "content": "Forces loyal to former Southwest State President Abdiaziz Hassan Mohamed Laftagareen have assumed control of Qansax-dheere district in the Bay region, sources said on [date]. The takeover occurred without immediate reports of clashes, though details remain limited.\n\nLaftagareen served as president of the Southwest State administration until he was replaced in a contentious electoral process. His tenure was marked by political tensions with the federal government and local opposition groups, leading to a prolonged standoff.\n\nThe district of Qansax-dheere, located in the Bay region, has previously witnessed intermittent control by various armed groups. The area's strategic position makes it significant for both regional trade and military movement.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this development signals a potential shift in the balance of power in the Southwest, a region that has seen repeated conflicts and political instability. Many diaspora members have family ties and investments in Bay and surrounding areas, and they closely monitor such changes for their implications on security and local governance.\n\nObservers note that the move could heighten tensions between Laftagareen's supporters and the current Southwest administration. The federal government has not yet issued a statement on the matter, and it remains unclear whether the takeover will be challenged.\n\nRead the original report from Horseed Media here: https://horseedmedia.net/ciidamada-laftagareen-oo-la-wareegey-degmada-qansax-dheere-ee-gobolka-baay/426301/",
