    "summary": "A spokesman for former South West President Abdiaziz Hassan Mohamed Laftagareen says forces loyal to him have recaptured the Qasaxdheere district in Bakool region. The claim could not be independently verified.",
    "content": "A spokesman for the former president of Somalia's South West state, Abdiaziz Hassan Mohamed Laftagareen, said on Thursday that forces loyal to the former leader had retaken the Qasaxdheere district in the Bakool region. The spokesman, Mohamed Hussein Hassan, made the claim in a post on social media, stating that the district was seized in the early hours of the morning.\n\nIn the post, Hassan said the \"historic district of Qasaxdheere\" had returned to the control of the South West state government. He called on residents across the region to remain calm. The statement did not provide details on casualties or the number of forces involved, and the claim has not been independently confirmed.\n\nLaftagareen served as president of South West state until he was removed from office in 2023 amid a political dispute with the federal government. Since then, he has retained a militia force known as the Darawiishta Koonfur Galbeed and has been engaged in a power struggle with the current regional administration. Qasaxdheere district has reportedly changed hands multiple times in recent months as competing forces vie for control.\n\nThe Somali diaspora, particularly those with ties to the South West region, has closely followed the volatile security situation in Bakool. Many diaspora members have family in the area and rely on informal networks for updates. The latest claim, if verified, could signal a renewed push by Laftagareen's forces to regain territory ahead of planned regional elections.\n\nObservers note that such claims are often difficult to verify due to limited access for independent journalists and the fluid nature of control on the ground. The South West administration has not yet issued a response to the spokesman's statement.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/10/08/afhayeenka-laftagareen-qasaxdheere-maanta-ayay-dib-ugu-soo-noqotay-gacanta-koonfur-galbeed/",
